> diff x^3
d/dx x^3 = 3x^2
  holds for every real x
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 2e-15)
> integrate x^2 from 0 to 1
∫ x^2 dx
  = x^3/3 + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [0, 1] (max difference 1.1e-16)
  from 0 to 1: F(1) - F(0) = 0.333333333333333
  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 0.333333333333333, estimated error 3.7e-15
  the two agree to 0
> expand (x+1)^5
  ucas: expand (x+1)^5
expand (x + 1)^5
  = x^5 + 5x^4 + 10x^3 + 10x^2 + 5x + 1
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> factor x^2-1
factor x^2 - 1
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
