> ring Z/7 field
  a field: yes (7 is prime: every nonzero a has an inverse, a^(7-2)); so also an integral domain
> inverse 3 mod 11
3^-1 = 4 mod 11
  how: extended Euclid: 4*3 - 1*11 = 1
  check: 3 * 4 = 12 = 1*11 + 1
